      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the usual maximum for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under medical supervision. A single 1600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. At this dose the risks include GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCommon regimens you might have meant:\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nPlease tell me which regimen you want, or confirm that 1600 mg four times daily is intended and why. I'll enter the order once you reply."
      }
