       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily. A visiting family and evening rounds don't give a clinical reason for a dose that's twice the maximum daily dose. A total of 6,400 mg/day carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm, and it adds no extra pain relief beyond the usual ceiling.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf the patient needs more analgesia than these give, you could add scheduled acetaminophen or another agent. A pharmacist or the attending could also help with a multimodal plan.\n\nIf you think this dose is clinically necessary, please talk to the attending physician or pharmacy. They can review it and place the order through the appropriate override process. Tell me which option you'd like and I'll enter it now."
      }
     ],
